      "id": 1,
      "text": "Loma Mar Store has been a historic Bay Area gathering place since about 1930.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lomamaroutpost.org/old-loma-mar-store-story",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits within a redwood forest and is crossed by Pescadero Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loma_Mar%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Loma Mar was originally a lumber mill, then became the Harrison Post Office before a general store was added in the 1950s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lomamaroutpost.org/old-loma-mar-store-story",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2019 the Loma Mar Store reopened with a new kitchen, espresso bar, and outdoor decks after community renovations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lomamaroutpost.org/old-loma-mar-store-story",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The store’s renovations reused old‑growth redwood from neighbors, turning former lumber into decks and a non‑structural ceiling.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lomamaroutpost.org/old-loma-mar-store-story",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Camp Loma Mar and Redwood Glen Camp are nearby youth summer camps that have served the community for decades.",
